{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01177 - MONDO_20320",
  "verbalization": "Idarubicin is shown to be associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation through multiple pathways, all of which involve Mitoxantrone. The evidence suggests that Idarubicin may be repurposed for this condition, as it is indicated in cases with Npm1, Cebpa, or Inv3(p21;q26.2) mutations, all of which are known to be associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia with Maturation. The shared indication with Mitoxantrone further supports a potential mechanistic link, as both drugs are known to inhibit DNA synthesis and induce apoptosis in leukemic cells. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship across different genetic subtypes of the disease. The presence of a common downstream target, Mitoxantrone, suggests that Idarubicin may act through a similar mechanism, potentially by targeting the same pathways or cellular processes that are dysregulated in Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Idarubicin could be a viable candidate for repurposing in this condition, provided further mechanistic validation is conducted.",
